{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\ncur=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='24f5b25cdc0e4a56a73a459285ab5e35-interpretation-0'][0]\nSR=\\\"ca148c05672f478186684b8c168d9601\\\"\nlim=[l for l in cur['limitations'] if not l.startswith(\\\"The caller's subsequent read of the FSM is not exercised\\\")]\nlim.insert(0,\\\"The end-to-end read is demonstrated in two of five trials of the latest probe: the stale read needs the verify to return success, and the other three trials answered leadership loss, in which case a correct caller would not go on to read the FSM at all.\\\")\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"3b823834c8cb46da98e77d8e988bf5d9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":list(dict.fromkeys(cur['source_ids']+[\\\"fsm_apply_values\\\",\\\"api_verify_doc\\\"])),\n \\\"executions\\\":{**cur['executions'], SR:[1,3,5,7,9]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(cur['rationale']+\\\" \\\"\n  \\\"The last limitation this account carried is now closed by a probe that reads the FSM instead of inferring the consequence. Each trial commits the value 'old' through the leader and waits for it to reach every node, partitions the leader, stalls its main loop, lets a successor at term 3 commit the value 'new', reconnects only the non-voter, and then reads the mock FSM on both nodes after the verify returns. All five trials show the divergence the consequence needs: the stalled leader's FSM still held 'old' while the successor held 'new' (comparisons at parsed indices 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9, the latter two confirming the successor's value), and in the two trials where the verify returned success (indices 1 and 7, reconnections 300ms and 450ms) a caller following the documented pattern would have read 'old' from a node it had just been told was still the leader, while the cluster's state was 'new'. The other three trials answered 'leadership lost while committing log', so the read only matters when the verify succeeds; the verdict remains the per-trial choice recorded earlier.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"f02f3b73bd1b44eba8471369b03da52b-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":2,\n   \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The FSM read at the stalled leader still holds the pre-partition value while the successor holds the new one, so a caller that acts on a successful verify reads state the cluster has moved past.\\\"}],\n \\\"answers\\\":cur['answers'],\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":cur['counterevidence'],\n \\\"limitations\\\":lim,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history']+\\\" A third revision, 6dde68d44bab41fda8cd5280bf6f72ac-experiment, reuses that harness and adds committed values plus reads of the mock FSM on both nodes, so its values are comparable with the earlier runs' endpoints and terms.\\\"}\nknowledge={\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"f02f3b73bd1b44eba8471369b03da52b-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":(\\\"A leader whose main loop is stalled past its lease can return VerifyLeader success while a successor already leads the cluster at a higher term, and a caller acting on that success reads state the cluster has moved past. Two executions of the endpoint probe show the overlap in twelve of twelve trials with eight successes (three of six, then five of six); a third execution reads the FSM directly and finds the stalled leader still holding the value committed before the partition while the successor holds the value committed after it, in all five trials, with the verify returning success in two of them (parsed indices 1 and 7) and leadership loss in the other three.\\\"),\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three voters plus one non-voter; the leader isolated from both other voters and from the non-voter while the request is registered; the leader's main loop then blocked inside StoreLogs for 900ms by a client Apply; the non-voter reconnected 250-500ms later; HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms, in-memory transports in one process, mock FSM recording applied commands.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"quorum_size\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"notify_all\\\",\\\"update_last_appended\\\",\\\"verify_vote\\\",\\\"lease_check\\\",\\\"lease_check_granularity\\\",\\\"fsm_apply_values\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"01617c5662f34c3eb21857602f6cac4f\\\":[1,3,5,7,9,11], \\\"2f645950e0334342b1f7392ed1c1f286\\\":[1,3,5,7,9,11], SR:[1,3,5,7,9]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"The premise is unchanged and the consequence is now measured rather than inferred: the earlier executions established the overlap and the endpoint, and this one reads the state machine on both nodes so the stale read is shown directly. The success rate across executions is recorded as it was rather than averaged into a single figure.\\\"),\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpreted the end-to-end stale-read probe, which closes the last limitation this question carried. All five trials show the FSM divergence the consequence needs - the stalled leader held the value committed before the partition while the successor held the value committed after it - and in the two trials where the verify returned success a caller following the documented pattern would have read the older value from a node just confirmed as leader. The three remaining trials answered leadership loss, so the read matters only when the verify succeeds and the per-trial choice is unchanged. The account gains the receipt in its executions, replaces the limitation that said the FSM read was not exercised, and lists the Fact it relies on, extended under its own id with the third execution and the values.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[knowledge],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
